{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context\nADR 0100 makes the immutable route registry and parser factories authoritative for command identity, grammar, and committed help. Twenty-one visible pure-intercept routes support `rebar <command> --help` but remain absent from overview help and fail under `rebar help <command>`. The `identity` child parsers disable their own help actions, so `rebar identity create --help` reaches top-level usage and exits with an error.\n\n## Plan\n- Make the help-backed predicate exactly `not route.hidden and not route.retired` in `scripts/gen_cli_help.py`, `src/rebar/_cli/_help_route.py`, `tests/interfaces/contracts/test_help_overview_coverage.py`, and `tests/interfaces/contracts/test_create_help_no_write_b8de.py`. Do not add route metadata.\n- Add nonblank parser descriptions to `reconcile.build`, `enrich.build`, `identity.build`, and `certs.build_trusted_env` so route-owned summaries populate overview help.\n- Move `_unwrap_usage` and `_collapse_metavars` from `scripts/gen_cli_reference.py` into `scripts/gen_cli_help.py`. Apply usage unwrapping only to intercept routes without explicit parser usage. Apply metavar normalization to intercept option lines before byte normalization. Preserve the explicit multiline `trusted-env` usage.\n- Expand the generator census through its public entry point. Do not test the private `_expected` helper. Generate one committed artifact for each newly help-backed route and regenerate `overview.txt`.\n- Widen top-level help pre-scan to every live visible route. Keep `_NESTED_INTERCEPTS` exactly `audit`, `config`, `identity`, `llm`, `prompt`, `criteria`, and `workflow` so nonleading child help reaches the owning parser or handler.\n- Enable help on the `identity create`, `identity use`, and `identity key` child parsers. Prove that each child returns child usage and exits successfully.\n- Keep the explicit `config validate --help` contract because `config validate` is handler-dispatched and has no populated argparse subparser action.\n- Keep parser-introspective nested-family coverage for argparse-backed families. Assert that the derived family set matches runtime ownership, then exercise each child-help path. Keep the 42-subprocess all-route contract in the held-out outer oracle.\n- Delete `_render_intercept` from `scripts/gen_cli_reference.py`. Make CLI reference generation consume `subcommand_help(route.name)` for every documented route. Update the two legacy expectations in `tests/unit/test_gen_cli_reference.py`.\n- Correct comments and docstrings that claim intercept routes lack committed help. The affected paths include `scripts/gen_cli_help.py`, `scripts/gen_cli_reference.py`, `src/rebar/_cli/_help_route.py`, `src/rebar/_cli/__init__.py`, `src/rebar/_cli/_llm_commands.py`, `src/rebar/_cli/_llm_eval_commands.py`, `src/rebar/_cli/_workflow_commands.py`, `src/rebar/_cli/_jira_onboard.py`, `src/rebar/_commands/verify_commit.py`, `src/rebar/_commands/verify_authorship.py`, `tests/interfaces/contracts/test_help_overview_coverage.py`, `tests/interfaces/contracts/test_create_help_no_write_b8de.py`, `tests/interfaces/contracts/test_parser_formatter_pinned.py`, `tests/interfaces/facades/test_central_mount_gate_ad9f.py`, `tests/unit/test_cli_registry_cutover_s6.py`, and `tests/unit/test_gen_cli_reference.py`.\n- Update affected expectations in `tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_plan_review_gate.py` and `tests/interfaces/facades/test_intercept_registry_cutover_s6_heldout.py`.\n- Retain `_OVERVIEW_OMIT` as exactly `bridge-fsck` and `bridge-probe`. Retain the test allowlist as exactly `help`, `bridge-fsck`, and `bridge-probe`.\n- Keep `tests/interfaces/contracts/test_parser_formatter_pinned.py` scoped away from pure-intercept parsers because generator normalization permits those parsers to retain the standard library formatter.\n- Regenerate package help and the CLI reference through their existing generators. The Python 3.11, 3.12, and 3.13 CI cells must pass the help drift check against the same committed bytes.\n- Do not add another router, parser, help source, mechanical writing-policy gate, or change to the Markdown-only reduced test policy.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Every live visible route outside the documented omit set appears exactly once in overview help.\n- [ ] `rebar help <command>` succeeds for every canonical pure-intercept route returned by the registry.\n- [ ] The pure-intercept help contract proves that no command handler executes.\n- [ ] The pure-intercept help contract proves that no ticket store is mounted or created.\n- [ ] `rebar help <command>` returns the matching committed artifact bytes.\n- [ ] Top-level `rebar <command> --help` returns the matching committed artifact bytes.\n- [ ] Every pure-intercept parser factory supplies a nonblank overview description.\n- [ ] The committed `trusted-env` usage banner preserves separate `add` and `revoke` lines.\n- [ ] Each CLI-reference pure-intercept syntax block equals the matching committed artifact.\n- [ ] A repository-wide semantic and string search reports zero `_render_intercept` references.\n- [ ] All four help-backed census sites use the live-visible predicate.\n- [ ] The exact overview exemptions remain `help`, `bridge-fsck`, and `bridge-probe`.\n- [ ] Hidden aliases and retired spellings remain absent from overview discovery.\n- [ ] `_NESTED_INTERCEPTS` equals `audit`, `config`, `identity`, `llm`, `prompt`, `criteria`, and `workflow`.\n- [ ] Every parser-introspectable nested family returns child-parser usage for each child.\n- [ ] `rebar identity create --help`, `rebar identity use --help`, and `rebar identity key --help` return their child usage and exit successfully.\n- [ ] `rebar config validate --help` reaches `build_validate` and returns validate child help.\n- [ ] Comments and test docstrings describe committed help ownership accurately.\n- [ ] The help drift check passes on supported Python versions.\n- [ ] The CLI-reference drift check passes.\n- [ ] No competing routing, parser, or help mechanism is introduced.\n- [ ] No mechanical writing enforcement is introduced.\n- [ ] The Markdown-only reduced test policy remains unchanged."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1787455610861167001,"uuid":"263a1e7a-8794-4df8-b508-ba7f190c7805"}